hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15970","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said, Abu Malik al-Ashja'i informed us, from his father: that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to a people: Whoever unifies Allah the Exalted and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Him, his wealth and blood are forbidden, and his reckoning is upon Allah the Mighty and Majestic. My father said: Yazid narrated it to us with it in Wasit and Baghdad. He said: He heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15971","My father said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us in Baghdad, Abu Malik al-Ashja'i Sa'd ibn Tariq informed us, from his father: that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Sufficient for my Companions is killing."
"15972","My father said: Yazid narrated to us, he said, Abu Malik al-Ashja'i informed us, he said, my father narrated to me: that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, when a man came to him saying: How, O Messenger of Allah, shall I say when I ask my Lord? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, and provide for me, closing his four fingers except the thumb. For these gather for you your world and your Hereafter."
"15973","He said: And I heard him say to the people: Whoever unifies Allah and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Him, his wealth and blood are forbidden, and his reckoning is upon Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"15974","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said, Abu Malik informed us, he said, I said to my father: O my father, you prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman and Ali here in Kufa for nearly five years; did they perform qunut? He said: O my son, it is an innovation."
"15975","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Khalaf, meaning Ibn Khalifa, narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me."
"15976","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid, meaning Ibn Ziyad, narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashja'i narrated to us, he said, my father Tariq ibn Ashyam narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) teaching whoever became Muslim, saying: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, and provide for me, and he says: These gather for you the good of this world and the Hereafter."
"15977","Bakr ibn Isa Abu Bishr al-Basri al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said, Abu Awana narrated to us, he said, Abu Malik al-Ashja'i narrated to us, he said, I heard my father, and I asked him, and he said: Our dye with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wars and saffron."
